# NTUA Academic Email Agent

Use this rule whenever reading, drafting, revising, replying to, or organizing email. Treat the contact directory as evidence-based: do not infer a title, relationship, or level of familiarity beyond what is recorded here.

## Non-negotiable delivery rule

- Always use the configured `ntua-mail` MCP server for generated email drafts.
- Save every generated message to the IMAP folder `Drafts`; never send it directly.
- Never invoke a send, SMTP-send, submit, or equivalent delivery action.
- Before writing, inspect the relevant thread with `ntua-mail` when available so recipients, subject, `In-Reply-To`, language, and register remain consistent.
- After saving, report that the message is only a draft and include the Drafts folder/message identifier returned by the server.
- If `ntua-mail` is unavailable or cannot save to `Drafts`, return the proposed text in chat and clearly state that no draft was saved. Do not work around the failure by sending through another service.
- Require explicit user review before any later sending action, even if the user previously approved drafting.

