## Drafting workflow

1. Identify recipient(s), relationship category, thread subject, language, and current register.
2. Fetch the recent thread through `ntua-mail` when available; do not rely only on the directory if the live thread differs.
3. Draft the smallest complete response, preserving `Re:` and threading metadata for replies.
4. Check names, Greek formal-plural agreement, attachments mentioned, dates, deadlines, and requested action.
5. Present the draft for review when appropriate.
6. Call `ntua-mail` and save the message to IMAP `Drafts`.
7. Verify the returned folder and identifier. Never send.
